====================================================================================================================================================================
                                              DevEN INTERACTIVE POWER SYSTEM SOLVER -- KCL REPORT
                                       KIRCHHOFF'S CURRENT & POWER BALANCE VERIFICATION PER BUS & BRANCH
Case: POWER TECHNOLOGIES STANDARD LARGE BENCHMARK CASE | Base MVA: 100.0  | Solver: DevEN Newton-Raphson | Iter: 11 | Converged: YES | Max dP: 0.0000   MW | Max dQ: 0.0000   Mvar
====================================================================================================================================================================
SIGN CONVENTION & SYMBOL LEGEND:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  QUICK SIGN RULE (POWER DIRECTION WITH RESPECT TO BUS TERMINAL):
    [+] POSITIVE (+) = Power is LEAVING the bus terminal (Outflow: flowing into a branch, consumed by load, absorbed by shunt).
    [-] NEGATIVE (-) = Power is ENTERING / COMING TOWARDS the bus terminal (Inflow: injected by generator, supplied from branch).

  DETAILED ELEMENT CONVENTIONS (MW, Mvar, MVA, Current in Amps):
    * BUS VOLTAGE:   V (pu) and V (kV) line-to-line magnitude; Angle (deg) referenced to Slack bus (0.0000 deg).
    * GENERATORS:    [+] Positive P / Q = Power GENERATED & INJECTED INTO the bus (Normal generator infeed).
                     [-] Negative P / Q = Power ABSORBED from the bus / EXPORTED TO GRID (e.g., Slack bus net export to external grid).
    * LOADS:         [+] Positive P / Q = Power CONSUMED & DRAWN FROM the bus (Normal customer load outflow).
                     [-] Negative P / Q = Power SUPPLIED into the bus (Negative load / rooftop DG infeed).
    * SHUNTS:        [+] Positive Q     = Capacitive reactive power INJECTED INTO bus (voltage boosting support, B > 0).
                     [-] Negative Q     = Inductive reactive power DRAWN FROM bus (voltage suppression reactor, B < 0).
                     [+] Positive P     = Active power conductance loss CONSUMED FROM bus (G > 0).
    * BRANCH FLOWS:  Both terminal flows (This Bus Terminal & Far Bus Terminal) displayed simultaneously:
                     [+] Positive P / Q = Power is LEAVING that bus terminal and flowing into the branch.
                     [-] Negative P / Q = Power is ENTERING / COMING TOWARDS that bus terminal from the branch.
                     Loss (MW / Mvar)   = Net branch dissipation: P_loss = P_this + P_far >= 0, Q_loss = Q_this + Q_far.
                     Load %             = MVA loading percentage against branch Rate A rating: (S / Rate_A) * 100%.
    * KCL BALANCE:   Net Bus Inflow (Gen - Load - Shunt) = Branch Outflow (Sum of branch flows leaving this bus).
                     Mismatch: dP = Net Bus Inflow - Total Branch Outflow = 0.0000 MW (Exact KCL active balance).
                               dQ = Net Bus Inflow - Total Branch Outflow = 0.0000 Mvar (Exact KCL reactive balance).
                               dI = Current mismatch in Amps = (dS * 1000) / (sqrt(3) * V_kV).
                     Status:   [KCL BALANCED [OK]] when |dP| < 0.01 MW and |dQ| < 0.01 Mvar.
====================================================================================================================================================================

